# UI work: Impeccable is required

These are hard requirements, not suggestions. Skipping any step is a failed task.

UI work means any change to a file that renders or styles the interface: `.css`, `.scss`, `.html`, `.tsx`, `.jsx`, `.astro`, `.svelte`, `.vue`, `.mdx`, layout and component files, design tokens, fonts, and images placed in the UI.

## Before you touch a UI file

1. Read `.cursor/skills/impeccable/SKILL.md` in full and follow it exactly. Do not work from memory of what Impeccable does.
2. Run its context step: `.cursor/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable context` from the repo root (add `--target <file or route>` when one surface is in scope). If the launcher fails, say so, then read `PRODUCT.md` and `DESIGN.md` directly.
3. Read `.cursor/skills/impeccable/reference/craft-floor.md` immediately before the first UI edit, as the skill says.
4. If `PRODUCT.md` is missing, run `/impeccable init` before new design work. If `DESIGN.md` is missing on an existing site, run `/impeccable document`.

## While you work

- `DESIGN.md` is the only source of visual truth: palette, type, spacing, radius, depth, motion. Where any other file (CLAUDE.md, a brief, an old comment) disagrees, DESIGN.md wins. If the task changes the design, update DESIGN.md in the same PR.
- Run `/impeccable critique` on the affected surface before any polish or refinement pass, and act on what it finds.
- Use the Impeccable command that fits the task (`polish`, `layout`, `typeset`, `colorize`, `quieter`, `bolder`, `animate`, `adapt`, `distill`, `harden`, or a new-work flow for a redesign). Read its reference file before using it.
- Treat a brief's exact values as intent. If a literal value would break the design or DESIGN.md, say so in the PR and propose the better value.

## Before you open the PR

1. Run the Impeccable finish review (the `impeccable-finish-reviewer` agent in `.cursor/agents/`, or `reference/degraded/finish-reviewer.md` when subagents are unavailable).
2. Run the detector on the changed UI files: `npx -y impeccable detect <files>`, and on the built HTML or the dev server URL when the site can run. Fix every error and explain any warning you keep.
3. Run `/site-finish` (`.cursor/skills/site-finish/SKILL.md`): interface and accessibility, motion and polish, and launch checks. Fix what it finds and put its report in the PR under `## Site finish`.
4. The PR body must contain the `## Impeccable` section from `.github/pull_request_template.md`, filled in: the commands that ran, the critique summary, and the detector and finish-review results. A missing section is a failed task.

## Skills in this repo

Only two: `.cursor/skills/impeccable` (how it looks) and `.cursor/skills/site-finish` (correct, accessible, polished, launch-ready). Impeccable and DESIGN.md win any disagreement.
